 "result_text": "Column widths are now correct. In your example, `h` and `mu` widen to fit values like `0.0`.\n\nThe cause was in `find_widths` in `src/pyRestTable/rest_table.py`. It measured each cell with `str(_ or '')`, so a falsy value like `0` counted as an empty string with width 0. I changed it to blank out only `None`.\n\nI checked it with a two-column version of your table (`h` and `mu`, rows `0, 0.0` and `0.0, 12.5`), and both columns come out wide enough. I didn't run your full nine-column example or the test suite.\n\nThe file changed on disk partway through my work. I read that as deliberate and left it alone.",
